    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Preordain before playing a land is a sequencing error. Gem3F has Island and Bloodstained Mire in hand. They should play the land first (Island), then cast Preordain. Playing the land first preserves optionality - if Preordain reveals something that changes what land they want to play, they've already committed. More importantly, playing Island first and keeping Bloodstained Mire in hand preserves the fetch land for later turns where Revolt enablement (for Fatal Push from opponent) or shuffle effects matter. However, the DRC surveil trigger from Preordain could influence what they want to do with their land drop, so there's some argument for casting first. But generally, playing lands before spells is correct sequencing since it costs nothing and preserves information advantage.",
