      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Thoughtseize over Fatal Push is debatable here. The opponent has a Dragon's Rage Channeler on the battlefield (tapped, likely attacked last turn) with 6 cards in graveyard - close to achieving delirium (they have Instant, Artifact, Sorcery, Land, Creature types visible, so DRC likely already has delirium and is a 3/3). Fatal Push would cleanly remove DRC (mana value 1, well within range), and with Polluted Delta in graveyard, revolt could even be enabled later by cracking Flooded Strand. However, Thoughtseize has merit - seeing the opponent's hand and stripping a key card (like Expressive Iteration or Mutagenic Growth) could be more impactful, especially since Kimi25 has Phelia coming down next turn and wants to protect it. The opponent also has an untapped Steam Vents, meaning they could have Lightning Bolt or other interaction. Thoughtseize lets you see what's coming and potentially strip removal before deploying Phelia. Still, removing DRC immediately with Fatal Push while it's the only threat on board, and saving Thoughtseize for when you have more information or when sequencing matters more, seems like a reasonable alternative line. This is close enough that it's debatable rather than clearly wrong.",
